  "recurring-data-view-design" [label="Review recurring\ndata requests and\ndesign faster\npreparation/views\nPARKED", shape=box, fillcolor="#f1f0ed", color="#93918c", tooltip="Original joint design remains open; unilateral bounded-pass completion claim withdrawn and Fix session informed. Following Fix's intervention, the EXISTING evidence worker produced concrete-view-alternatives-20261004.md, now integrated and rendered through the existing server: exact CV/OTel request-result/intervention specimens, six joined recurring needs, retrospective versus incremental preparation plus separate interpretation, upkeep/invalidation/freshness, measured latency and useful combinations. Original CVs and disputed timing-chain report are absent. Historical telemetry remains explicitly a retained corrected response; original raw scratch report is no longer present. Packet does not establish a complete census, adequate-context reviewer quality or accepted final design. Existing capabilities can be reused; implementation and unapproved programmes remain stopped.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Jörn requested log review and joint brainstorming/design. Bounded source inspection and isolated probe only; approval precedes deployment. No source build, new permanent service, config activation or daemon restart. Jörn approved applying the messaging rules to project guidance; Stop-hook activation remains unapproved. Jörn selected skill placement conditional on clarity to fresh agents; bounded fresh-context checks completed.\nnext_step: Resource stop relayed by Fix orchestration: current analysis/planning stopped and the running evidence child interrupted. Existing artifacts and unfinished joint-design obligation preserved. Resume only on renewed instruction; no completion, new programme or spending approval implied. Separately authorized reset timers are untouched.\nSources: docs/codex.md, docs/coordination/README.md"];
  "codex-passive-usage-attribution" [label="Complete passive\naccounting and\nongoing-work\nresource awareness\nREADY", shape=box, fillcolor="#fff7dc", color="#aa8a31", tooltip="Technical assessment/repairs and bounded delivery checks returned; Jörn graded this attempt FAIL. Earlier root/supervisor completion claims do not establish human acceptance of the workflow. Retained evidence: owned-response/fork/counter repairs,20 focused native-reader tests, selected-root projection compatibility, fresh-agent command/interpretation discovery, three root/worker usage-note receipts, and actual time/context-tool delivery. C hook remains withdrawn and inactive. Repeated objective drift, rejected overbuilding, scope takeover and premature endings remain session failures; useful component checks do not cancel that verdict. At closure Jörn questioned giving up and explicitly requested notifying Fix Codex thread orchestration. Root’s earlier ending was its own choice, not an explicit user cancellation. The requested notification was accepted through native tool-output transport by existing orchestration thread01a103dc-762f-7ef1-a094-4b0247b290ff; receipt not yet verified.\nplan_gap: Workflow acceptance failed for this attempt. No further root execution or invented approval question selected at closure. Permanent/all-agent coverage, native export deduplication, active-work/task joins and quota/billing conversion remain unestablished. Technical artifacts are retained without a PASS/readiness claim.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Jörn requested checking available scripts and applicable other-session ownership for passive resource attribution. Bounded read-only observation and correction of an attribution grouping defect; no quota experiment, new service or budget enforcement selected. Follow-up bounded readiness review covers discoverability, automation, session-log attribution, trust and fork behavior; it does not activate a new service, hook, skill, goal or quota experiment. Jörn explicitly instructed fixing the reproduced defects at 21:13 UTC on 3 October. Reporting at task start/handoff was rejected; no automatic delivery mechanism was approved. Jörn explicitly objected to stopping with incomplete work at 21:25 UTC and directed continued workflow completion, allowing a specific question/blocker when necessary. Bounded implementation and delivery investigation continue; config approval boundary remains. Completion is scoped to the original local script-readiness/fork/discoverability/interpretation questions and subsequent supervised ongoing-work observation; no broader service, scientific run or spending selected.\nnext_step: Existing Fix orchestration owner receives the failed-attempt result and Jörn’s objection to giving up; no assignment transfer, extra spending or cancellation inferred from sending this report.\nSources: scripts/subtree-usage.py, scripts/subtree-usage.md, scripts/test_subtree_usage.py, scripts/coordination-load.py, scripts/test_coordination_load.py, docs/coordination/README.md, docs/codex.md, scripts/usage-awareness.py, scripts/test_usage_awareness.py, docs/codex-config-proposals.md"];
