  "__completed" [label="DONE · owners released\nShared coordination\nLocal guidance\nWorkstation OTel\nSkill proposal\nKnowledge proposal\nSemantic project map\nSupport-route proposal\nAccounting proposal\nProject completion map\nCode and evidence\nSource repairs\nClaims supported\nFrozen candidate\nLoad supervision\nIntake approach comparison\nProblem-knowledge sources\nCheck readable browser delivery of the goal map\nCompare mechanisms for making problem knowledge usable\nTry existing knowledge routes for a communication problem\nCodex config / source\nAbsolute-path workstation file viewer\nBounded root scope supervision\nReconcile withdrawn usage-hook references\nAudit native telemetry completion accounting\nVerify fresh-agent resource-measurement discovery\nPostmortem of recent root-session failures\nDesign a valuable five-hour Codex task and launch prompt\nAttempt the expiring Codex reset at 04:00 Berlin\nPrepare concrete symmetric-partner exposition candidate\nResolve the regular-heptagon calibration lead\nUnify symmetric-partner calibration for odd regular factors\nCheck local persistence and one exact rational control\nCorrect the pentagon certificate packet proof route\nFoundations and finite-capacity proof exposition\nRepository navigation and evidence ownership\nIndependent cross-chapter claim review\nDeliver revised thesis PDF and repository before 04:00 Berlin\nIndependent product-theorem review\nPreserve interrupted work and prepare an honest restart handoff\nAssemble and integrate one checked candidate\nIndependently review science, code contract and exact PDF\nObserve actual integration queue and orchestration outcomes\nRepair evidence routing and reproduction documentation\nRepair and inspect selected PDF layout\nCorrect wider action-window enumeration contract\nIndependently inspect changed mathematical interfaces\nComplete figure reproduction routes and integrate useful repairs\nIndependently check remaining empirical evidence and new output\nCheck independent production-capacity mathematical anchors\nSupervise original objective, substantive progress and stop\nReproduce six empirical figure assets\nReproduce seven structural and visualization assets\nIndependently audit retained DS claims\nExecute printed HKO appendix and full certificate\nCheck thesis build in a second cached tool environment\nConsolidate worktrees onto main\nDiscuss research completion and supervision controls\nRepair post-consolidation access, inputs and stale references\nLocate live research questions and existing payoff judgments\nRetrieve taste and orchestration feedback that changes selection\nVerify current reset job without redemption or scheduling\nPrepare and challenge 4–6 research ideas with resource alternatives\nVerify quota and provide a cheap reusable read-only check\nLocate latest F10/F11 proof statements and Pro provenance\nCheck newest ProF11proof statement and consequential implications\nRepair known issues before human research-calibration review\nExpand predicted scientific outcomes and concrete conditional labor\nAccept F≤11 theorem or identify exact gap\nFind worthwhile extremality/equality route\nFind distinct strong geometric mechanism\nCompare actual science and recommend next allocation\nSupervise actual execution, value and pending decisions\nRetain acceptedF11 result with source/PDF caveats\nTest direct global fixedP5 cover route\nRetain accepted equiangularGLOBAL theorem\nProve sharp global bound on nonconformal fan family\nSharp global bound for HKO-angle deformed normal fan\nRetain aligned-fan theorem and P* partial facet-birth results\nProve coupled moving endpoint for P* p1 tilt\nRetain accepted HKO-angle global theorem\nVerify pruning and measure orientation-wide proof complexity\nComplete exact joint denominator cells across orientation\nRetain accepted restricted moving endpoint theorem\nProve sharp global bound/equality in explicit orientation-wide family\nRetain accepted orientation-wide result and reconcile research view\nMeasure supplied contacts for whole-facet balanced response\nTest complete regular P* facet bank with exact response or separator\nRetain new pointwise balanced P* response and exact caveats\nCheck exact weighted W curvature for new balanced response\nReconcile accepted curvature gate and remaining ambient gap\nProve uniform moving-old control near the new generic split direction\nVerify wider fan reduction to finite quadratic target on linear cone\nRetain accepted new P* ambient direction patch\nRetain accepted general-matrix finite cone reduction\nReplace collaboration skills and add companion design memory\nReplace leftover T3 file-server favicon\nAssess incident intake and companion-note coverage\nReview all project skills before Jörn’s sweep\nIntegrate reset investigation into skill maintenance\nContinue skill review with concrete resource and naming candidates\nComplete integrated skill review before Jörn’s sweep\nFresh-clone readiness and agent coordination audit\nExact-text independent message approval\nCodex app-server skill for shell/cloud agents\nA: Repo-only cloud readiness\nB: Remaining harness and collaboration\n9 October agent-account session: Jörn FAIL verdict", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#e7f1e8", color="#93918c", tooltip="Separate coordination, browser views and reusable knowledge\nCanonical coordination and browser source contract complete; five HTTP checks passed. Prior Chrome inspection unavailable.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md, docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/coordination/handoff.md\n\nRoute process knowledge into project collaboration guidance\nLocal collaboration rules and knowledge routing complete; link/state checks passed. Behavioral and post-compaction performance untested. On 3 October, added Jörn-requested continuity guidance: brief acknowledgments do not stop unfinished authorized work; completion, explicit stopping and visible required-input boundaries remain. Rationale retained in commentary; behavioral effect untested.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected. Jörn subsequently requested the narrow acknowledgment/continuation correction in the Codex walkthrough on 3 October.\nSources: AGENTS.md, AGENTS.md.commentary.md, docs/knowledge/README.md\n\nSet up authorized workstation-only OpenObserve telemetry\nLive workstation logs/traces/metrics API-verified after daemon restart. Host implementation complete; maintenance belongs to ~/.dotfiles/INSTALL.md. Browser login unverified.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/development-environments.md, docs/coordination/otel-design.md\n\nPrepare repository-owned skill migration\nReviewable local skill/discovery migration proposal returned; planner assignment ended. Candidate, activation and fresh-client acceptance remain unselected.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/skill-migration-plan.md\n\nPlan process-knowledge cleanup and behavioural evaluation\nReviewable two-link cleanup and bounded forward-pilot proposal returned; planner assignment ended. Cleanup and pilot remain unselected.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/knowledge-evaluation-plan.md\n\nSemantic msc-math project map dashboard\nSemantic DOM portfolio view completed in dedicated design session: whole msc-math goal, completion branches, interactive outcome/status/owner/blocker/scope/evidence/next-step nodes and shared prerequisite links. Live desktop/390px and320px fixture checked; no horizontal overflow.15second refresh preserves open state/focus. Root integrated source/dependency checks and8 HTTP tests.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md\n\nDefine support and handoff routes across selected environments\nRead-only supported-route matrix returned: local .agents source plus proposed Claude links/import; retained packets and manual host handoff initially. Independent-thread live delivery and SSH persistence remain unverified; Codex Cloud privileged-image/R2 bootstrap assumptions are not validated for Claude.\nplan_gap: Claude fresh-clone setup/discovery, cloud-to-host handoff, remote-device review access and reconnect/session continuity have no agreed acceptance route. Required support versus explicitly deferred capabilities is unresolved.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/development-environments.md, docs/coordination/skill-migration-plan.md\n\nDefine truthful usage and spending observations\nRead-only recommendation returned: current.json and retained outcomes own durable PM state; OpenObserve is diagnostic. Optional explicit packet-event JSONL-to-OTel helper only if selected; no broker/database. Token/time observations are not billing; quota/USD unknown and independent-root/cloud usage is not covered.\nplan_gap: Comparable cloud/Pro usage, semantic task/message journaling and budget-enforcement mechanics are undefined. Numeric thresholds are not agreed; the selected delivery may explicitly defer automation.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: AGENTS.md.commentary.md, docs/development-environments.md\n\nWhole-project completion map and dependency projection\nWhole msc-math outcome/dependency map retained: workflow subproject, thesis support/prose and human PASS, code/evidence, reproduction, actual delivery/archive and closure. Twelve independent read-only candidates plus optional research/writing routes are visible without execution authorization. Semantic dashboard is primary; DOT/SVG source-hash projection checks pass.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md\n\nRetained implementation and artifact claims match their support\nCurrent candidate code/artifact claims received bounded source, count, path and API-contract review; two numerical defects repaired, all 52 literal local path occurrences resolve, retained exact evidence verified. Flow production correspondence remains explicitly bounded; this is not a whole-implementation proof.\nplan_gap: No need for blanket code cleanup or a universal solver formalization; inspect exactly what retained claims require.\nproject: evidence\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped. The oct04-candidate restart authorizes bounded thesis/repository improvement until 02:00 UTC; human PASS, public release and university submission are not implied.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/acceptance-numerical.md, docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/acceptance-source-review.md\n\nClose surviving source repairs and reader-comment dispositions\nPrior seven source obligations remain dispositioned; continuation also supplies missing prediction methods and fixes rational/dyadic wording. No open blocking finding in the bounded independent patch review; human PASS and overall DS scope remain unknown.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped. The oct04-candidate restart authorizes bounded thesis/repository improvement until 02:00 UTC; human PASS, public release and university submission are not implied.\nnext_step: Bounded run closed; preserved evidence and remaining project limits govern any later authorized continuation.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/ds-comment-disposition.md, docs/history/thesis-continuation-2026-10-04/acceptance-review.md\n\nAudit selected theorem and empirical wording against evidence\nAll 11 required areas mapped against selected sources, final PDF and evidence. Independent bounded reviews found no remaining blocking scoped finding; fixed-facet/equality/upper-section, empirical and conditional-flow limitations preserved. No unrestricted verification or human PASS implied.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped. The oct04-candidate restart authorizes bounded thesis/repository improvement until 02:00 UTC; human PASS, public release and university submission are not implied.\nnext_step: Bounded run closed; preserved evidence and remaining project limits govern any later authorized continuation.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-continuation-2026-10-04/acceptance-review.md, docs/history/thesis-continuation-2026-10-04/acceptance-manifest.json\n\nAssemble and inspect one exact reader-facing candidate\nFinal101-page candidate d27e2f53… binds61thesis files at source00d03ceb… and independent acceptance81f5d804…. Complete page-level review/all11required-area map; prior100-page artifact preserved. The commit containing this state retains the delivery.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped. The oct04-candidate restart authorizes bounded thesis/repository improvement until 02:00 UTC; human PASS, public release and university submission are not implied.\nnext_step: Bounded run closed; preserved evidence and remaining project limits govern any later authorized continuation.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-continuation-2026-10-04/candidate-manifest.json, docs/history/thesis-continuation-2026-10-04/acceptance-manifest.json\n\nLoad checker and bounded watch outcome\nRead-only checker integrated and independently reviewed; 13 focused tests pass. Bounded observer interrupted after Jörn ended the discussion; full planned watch not established. Last retained 17:30:52Z snapshot had no errors/advisory signals; overload and semantic queue unknown. Observer role lacked native send tools; TUI report transport worked. Early second observation revealed interrupted-sleep cadence error, corrected to absolute targets. This closes the implementation/interrupted-watch packet only; ongoing coordination burden supervision remains the coordinator’s responsibility, with no validated semantic queue measurement.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Selected bounded implementation and supervision; four observations over about twelve minutes, no permanent service or thesis execution.\nnext_step: Use the checker during selected ongoing work; workload assessment must include undelivered obligations, messages and review/integration burden. Quiet telemetry and a low worker count do not establish low load.\nSources: scripts/coordination-load.py, scripts/test_coordination_load.py, docs/coordination/README.md\n\nCompare intake approaches before selecting one\nFresh-context agent returned candidates starting from concern coverage, an incident trace, or a fresh-consumer handoff test. Includes useful outputs, uncertainties, failure/switch signs and relative unmeasured costs. This closes only the assigned comparison return; value, novelty and approach selection remain unestablished.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: Bounded preliminary brainstorming following Jörn’s request to discuss approaches before choosing promising ones. No implementation, configuration change, paid trial, scientific producer or further delegation.\nnext_step: Discuss the candidates and assumptions in the parent conversation before selecting any probe. Prior attempts should inform novelty/value claims.\nSources: docs/history/coordination/20261003-project-repair-user-report.md, AGENTS.md.commentary.md, docs/coordination/intake-approach-options.md\n\nMap prior problem knowledge and compare evidence-maintenance approaches\nBounded source-map, evidence-recovery/evaluation and coordination-topology comparisons returned. No topology is established necessary or superior; recommendations remain hypotheses. Completion covers the assigned returns only.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: Preliminary source mapping and discussion within the repair intake. No raw-rollout crawl, active incident migration, evaluations, substantial execution, configuration changes or further delegation.\nnext_step: Retain source-qualified return and compare concrete paths with Jörn; do not infer a selected incident architecture or evaluated remedy.\nSources: docs/history/coordination/20261003-project-repair-user-report.md, docs/knowledge/README.md, AGENTS.md.commentary.md, docs/coordination/intake-approach-options.md, docs/coordination/problem-knowledge-source-map.md\n\nCheck readable browser delivery of the goal map\nLuna corrected default SVG scaling after observing tiny labels. Isolated headless Chrome verified the served page, node selection and necessity filter. Wide graph requires horizontal scrolling. This establishes presentation behavior, not the model or intervention efficacy.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: 3 October authorized bounded brainstorming, source retrieval and information-producing probes. No substantial execution, host configuration change or thesis restart.\nnext_step: Review and revise the provisional conceptual map as discussion changes its claims.\nSources: scripts/render-goal-map.py, docs/coordination/graphs/goal-map.html\n\nCompare mechanisms for making problem knowledge usable\nCandidate report compares decision-triggered retrieval, task-entry context delivery and change-driven reconciliation. Each includes probes and failure signs; no activation or efficacy established.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: 3 October authorized bounded brainstorming, source retrieval and information-producing probes. No substantial execution, host configuration change or thesis restart.\nnext_step: Use the comparison to choose a concrete information-producing probe, checking past attempts and application failures.\nSources: docs/coordination/problem-knowledge-interventions.md\n\nTry existing knowledge routes for a communication problem\nFresh consumer recovered scoped cases and local positive interaction evidence, but no general effective remedy. Message-review skill records a negative live trial with an unlinked host-only antecedent. This is one observed retrieval pass, not a general inventory or causal diagnosis.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: 3 October authorized bounded brainstorming, source retrieval and information-producing probes. No substantial execution, host configuration change or thesis restart.\nnext_step: Candidate next investigation: recover an exact disputed-answer/intervention case; do not repeat the failed skill as an established fix.\nSources: docs/coordination/problem-knowledge-probe.md\n\nDocument Codex implementation and make project overrides explicit\nRelease-matched Codex reference and source-only refresh helper complete at CLI/daemon 0.160.0. Project agent limits and selected flags are explicit; model/effort remain host-owned. Maintenance and explicit config-edit approval rules are documented. All 154 flags have generated registry descriptions, candidate consumer links, fresh values, project overrides, provenance and first-pass screening; historical runtime versions remain unknown. Two bounded source reviewers returned time/budget/cache and encryption findings, integrated by this coordinator with no worker obligation remaining. Source inspection establishes the legacy timeout no-op, model-selected V2 semantics and lack of a supported encryption-disable toggle; production plaintext-forcing patch efficacy is unverified. Jörn approved the automatic time-reminder setting as a provisional trial: 60-second system-clock reminders after user/tool output, with interruptible sleep available. Applied config comments record that he considers this cadence fast; usefulness and cache/cost effects are unmeasured. Jörn also explicitly approved the provisional context trial B: context metadata/tools and a 20,000-token pre-compaction warning, with the history/notes extension off. Developer-message retention, mailbox deferral and deferred-tool world state were not selected because no concrete solved problem was identified. Rollout budget remains off; its injected messages count remaining weighted tokens and it has no uncapped count-up-only mode or dedicated flag-registered query tool. Existing get_goal reports cumulative goal token/time usage with optional cap and automatic continuation; no goal or new meter was selected. Schema and fresh loader checks passed; inventory regenerated. Existing-thread adoption and runtime benefit remain unverified. No host config edit, build, restart or paid cache pilot. Runtime observation at22:14UTC: this running root received repeated timestamp developer messages and context-window metadata; get_context_remaining returned120014. Worker reconciled only docs/codex.md and docs/codex-config-proposals.md; root reviewed. Delivery in this root is observed; exact config provenance/cadence, threshold warning, other agents, continuity and benefit remain unverified.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Jörn requested a repository documentation/source-navigation reference and explicit repo config overrides on 3 October; then explicitly excluded model/effort from repo overrides. Source checkout is for inspection only. No host config edit, CLI build/install, daemon restart or paid trial. Jörn subsequently explicitly approved enabling the proposed automatic time reminders, marked provisional/in test, in this thread; context-budget proposal B remains unapproved. Jörn explicitly approved enabling and provisionally marking