edgment failed. Final narrow assessment found original local passive-attribution/discovery/delivery obligations complete, with no user-only decision. Review points respected; no permanent/sustained-effectiveness or universal route guarantee.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Bounded work under Jörn’s request for supervision and correction of root derailment; no permanent mechanism, config activation, scientific run or paid API.\nnext_step: Assignment reviewed and released. Reuse supervision when useful in later selected work; observation responsibility does not end at conversation boundaries.\nSources: docs/coordination/current.json, docs/coordination/handoff.md\n\nReconcile withdrawn usage-hook references\nWorker corrected only four stale C references in docs/codex.md, docs/coordination/README.md, scripts/README.md and scripts/subtree-usage.md. Root reviewed the withdrawal disposition. Historical candidate retained; no activation approval pending; counters/on-demand command remain and parent outcome is open. No code/config/guidance change.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Bounded work under Jörn’s request for supervision and correction of root derailment; no permanent mechanism, config activation, scientific run or paid API.\nnext_step: Assignment reviewed and released.\nSources: docs/codex.md, docs/coordination/README.md, scripts/subtree-usage.md\n\nAudit native telemetry completion accounting\nReproduced and fixed raw SSE polling rows being treated as invalid usage completions and erasing known cache-write0. Raw observations now separate; malformed/partial/unmarked missing usage still diagnosed, raw-only tokens unknown.20 focused tests pass. Recent-root-only whitelist query observed omitted absent fields and29 valid parsed completions with no projection/regression errors. Raw-SSE branch source/fixture verified, not live exercised; native export dedup remains unverified and no live duplicate charging established.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Bounded diagnosis and same-worker repair continuing the selected local resource-attribution outcome; no config/service, native dedup guess, paid call or other project expansion.\nnext_step: Reviewed result retained in usage contract and tests; worker released. Recheck native dedup only if separately selected or new evidence warrants it.\nSources: scripts/coordination-load.py, scripts/test_coordination_load.py, scripts/subtree-usage.md\n\nVerify fresh-agent resource-measurement discovery\nOne isolated read-only consumer found README->coordination guide->usage contract, gave correct commands and interpretations of count-up units, fork ownership, walltime including idle, manual/supervised delivery, quota/billing and coverage limits. It found stale --help prototype status; assigned worker corrected only docstring/help, reviewed with --help and diffcheck. No new skill, service or behavioral feature.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Bounded verification of Jörn’s original discoverability/interpretation question within selected local resource work.\nnext_step: Fresh-consumer findings integrated; assignment released.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md, scripts/subtree-usage.md, scripts/usage-awareness.py\n\nPostmortem of recent root-session failures\nCompleted and indexed in canonical main: eight-root causal postmortem, retained evidence and runtime-source checks, lean reusable knowledge, two bounded evaluations with null/adverse results and limits preserved. Original early submission was withdrawn and materially extended. Historical outputs remain with their recorded owners; no live remedy or thesis programme was launched.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: User authorized all available included Codex quota, including parallel subagents, until 2026-10-04 01:54:26 UTC (03:54 Berlin), and no additional paid usage. Scope explicitly MSc/Codex workflow root sessions only; no live remediation/thesis execution.\nSources: docs/history/session-postmortem-2026-10-04/REPORT.md, docs/knowledge/session-failures-2026-10-03.md, docs/history/session-postmortem-2026-10-04/OUTPUTS.md\n\nDesign a valuable five-hour Codex task and launch prompt\nAfter Jörn challenged the reviewer set, fresh review_coverage mapped decision coverage and proposer/reviewer dependence; fresh allocation_challenge compared required thesis scope, alternatives and critical path. Changed plan to three production lanes (product/symmetric account, variation, numerical example) plus foundations/assembled-reader owner; COVER-L only conditional opportunity. Fresh reviewer checked revision and recommended KEEP, with explicit crossed reviewers including foundations edits. Coordinator ran two bounded offline public-capacity tests, both passed (scalar/exact comparison and exact-enumeration action window). Full reviewed prompt and coverage/preflight evidence retained in docs/coordination/five-hour-portfolio-prompt.md and five-hour-review-coverage.md. No substantial scientific execution or human acceptance. At orchestration request, a standalone remaining-window adaptation is retained in docs/coordination/remaining-window-thesis-proposal.md: existing broader odd-polygon theorem candidate, variation section, retained certified example, and assembled PDF/insertion patch. Timing and broader-theorem emphasis are not a newly independently reviewed allocation; no production or human acceptance. Jörn rejected the four-worker cap as unsubstantiated. Revised standalone proposal inventories ten content units, three proof/source reviewers, one assembled reader and two delegated integrators (16 workers plus supervising root); compares four/eight/sixteen without claiming measured capacity. Four detailed allocation messages delivered; final artifact-update notification failed transport. No agents or production launched.\nproject: msc-math\nauthorization: User selected task/prompt design and agent value assessment. Bounded preliminary source discovery, design and reviews, including a review-set coverage check and two existing offline public-API fixture tests. No five-hour package, retained producer overwrite, active manuscript change or paid spending authorized/launched.\nnext_step: Four-worker cap withdrawn. Standalone remaining-window proposal now has 16 disjoint roles, supported source/output table, 4/8/16 comparison and delegated mathematical/evidence integration. Orchestration owns sole approval; no substantial execution approved. New timing and 16-role allocation are not independently validated throughput or PASS claims. Final artifact notification failed; use shared server/source fallback. Receiving root ownership remains conditional.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md, docs/coordination/remaining-window-thesis-proposal.md\n\nAttempt the expiring Codex reset at 04:00 Berlin\nRead-only consolidation check of host result.json records primary outcome=reset; claude-result.json records fallback outcome=skipped. This supersedes the pending timer observation. No redemption or new account request was made during consolidation. Historical one-date authorization is not standing authority.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: User authorized the conditional 04:00 attempt and requested considering a scheduled Claude Code session as an additional route. Primary and bounded Claude fallback use one logical pinned earned-reset redemption with the identical credit/key. Claude fallback may launch one session for at most 120 seconds after local failure; only the exact existing script command is allowed. No other credit, purchase, login, semantic-refusal retry, repository edits or other agents/model turns are authorized for this job.\nnext_step: Both timers trigger at 04:00 Berlin. Primary writes private result.json; the now-authenticated Claude fallback skips success or server refusal and otherwise attempts the same pinned command after local failure, recording claude-result.json. Host must be awake/online. Actual server acceptance is established only