e/version metadata, plus bounded review. Scope includes necessary project discovery/config and caller migration; no global deployment, broader September semantic ports or substantial experiment.\nSources: .agents/skills/README.md, docs/knowledge/collaboration-guidance-design-2026-10-05.md, docs/coordination/skill-replacement-validation-20261005.md\n\nReplace leftover T3 file-server favicon\nAdded a neutral document SVG at /files/favicon.svg?v=1 and explicit favicon links on generated listings, Markdown and text views. Worker restarted only msc-math-files.service; live HTTPS checks pass for the icon and four pages (200, correct content types/lengths, no-store). Eight existing viewer tests and diff checks pass. Uncommitted; existing tabs may need refresh. Root-host cached-icon history remains unproven.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Jörn explicitly requested the favicon fix and subagent delegation. Only favicon and directly necessary serving changes, with focused verification; preserve unrelated host/project work.\nSources: scripts/serve-files.py\n\nAssess incident intake and companion-note coverage\nInspected current incident-log and nine project packages. One fresh explicit synthetic intake preserves uncertainty and continues task; real bounded session intake retained in agent-skills default owner. Earlier root did not invoke intake on user-identified failures; automatic triggering/downstream benefit remain unknown. Added meaningful incident-log design notes and maintenance link; four of nine packages now have notes, optional recommendation leaves five without. No broad semantic ports or expensive evaluation.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Jörn asked whether incident-log is useful/works, what session incidents are relevant, and whether project skills follow companion-note guidance. Bounded assessment/capture/check and meaningful local maintenance note; no blanket skill rewrites.\nSources: docs/history/incident-log-evaluation-20261006/README.md, .agents/ski