/SKILL.md, docs/history/skill-presweep-20261006/README.md\n\nComplete integrated skill review before Jörn’s sweep\nIntegrated full skill sweep completed. Reconciled maintained sources; added explicit dispositions for eight retained session failures; independent content/application reviews and one three-input continuation forward return retained. Installed local codex-resources guidance and renamed cloud workflow to codex-cli-claude-cloud with callers/discovery links migrated. Incident unavailable-owner fallback and fetch slug/feed/comment handling repaired. Ten frontmatters, offline helpers, shell syntax and 87 local links pass. Bounded public query observations retained. Fresh runtime discovery, reliable automatic behavior, cloud execution and persistent reset recovery are not established. Changes uncommitted.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Jörn requested full skill-set work, independent review and continuation, with bounded preliminary tests/comparison under existing maintenance scope. No live redemption, timer/config reset mutation, substantial evaluation programme or global deployment.\nnext_step: Review package delivered for Jörn’s sweep. No required user decision blocks this completed assignment. Wider behavioral acceptance and production reset-controller execution remain separate, unselected work.\nSources: docs/history/skill-presweep-20261006/README.md, .agents/skills/README.md, docs/history/skill-presweep-20261006/behavior-dispositions.md, docs/history/skill-presweep-20261006/continuation-forward/output/review.md\n\nFresh-clone readiness and agent coordination audit\nBounded factual source/data/build investigation retained, but Jörn rejected the activity-oriented chat delivery and subsequent amendments. Not an accepted assessment or complete working-state outcome. Later selected work implements exact-text independent message review; original findings remain evidence with their caveats.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Jörn requested a new working-state assessment on 8 October. Bounded inspection and independent review; no substantial execution, config activation, account operation or thesis restart.\nSources: docs/coordination/cloud-harness-audit-20261008/README.md, docs/coordination/cloud-harness-audit-20261008/clean-thesis-build.json\n\nExact-text independent message approval\nSelected shared-standard revision complete: AGENTS review section29->7lines; one549-word skill read by sender/reviewer; no separate prompt template or mandatory schema/hash/repeated-text receipt. Named native reviewer approves frozen candidate version with substantive findings; exact text/attribution/context and renewed-review requirements retained. Old verifier/tests/receipts explicitly historical. /root/shared_review approved exact delivery and found no consequential source omission in one no-tool response. Structural/link/diff checks are limited evidence; no enforced delivery block, measured savings or future reliability claimed.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Jörn requested making communication guidance actionable with a named subagent approving exact prepared-message text and a prepared review workflow. Local instructions/checker, bounded native review and tests; no separately governed config change or platform deployment.\nSources: AGENTS.md, docs/coordination/message-reviews/README.md\n\nCodex app-server skill for shell/cloud agents\nRepo-local codex-app-server skill and shell client integrated with Claude discovery. Workstation 0.161.0 create/disconnect/follow-up/fork/title/archive/restore checks and 13 offline regression tests passed. Fresh Claude-cloud install/device login/network/lifetime unverified; no new login grant or host daemon restart. Existing one-shot cloud CLI workflow retained.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Jörn requested repo-local daemon-backed skill/wrapper on 8 October 2026, explicitly a skill rather than the OpenAI Claude Code plugin. Implementation and bounded tests only; no device grant or substantial workload selected.\nnext_step: Use in a selected cloud task; authenticate only after authorization for that particular device grant. Fresh-cloud behavior remains unverified.\nSources: .agents/skills/codex-app-server/SKILL.md, .agents/skills/codex-app-server/references/design-notes.md, docs/development-environments.md\n\nA: Repo-only cloud readiness\nInitial A inspection/preparation complete: coherent readiness assessment and concrete completion route, approved for exact delivery by /root/cloud_a_review. Core source work is close to portable; current skill delivery, image-coupled credential-first bootstrap, conditional host workflows and historical retention exceptions remain. Fresh-target acceptance and implementation are not established. No cloud install/login, artifact payload download/publication, producer or project config/skill-body change. Added assessment/receipt serving entries and refreshed coordination projection.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Jörn requested two new sessions on8October. Initial bounded investigation/problem development; no substantial execution, research restart or config authority inferred.\nnext_step: Implementation and disposable Claude-cloud acceptance remain proposals, not selected execution. A session 01a11bb5-f148-79a2-9bf8-38507146196d owns direct follow-through if Jörn selects continuation; B remains independent.\nSources: docs/coordination/handoffs/20261008-ab-split/A-cloud.md, docs/coordination/cloud-readiness-20261008/assessment.md, docs/coordination/cloud-readiness-20261008/inspection.json\n\nB: Remaining harness and collaboration\nInitial bounded B assessment complete and exact final-v1 approved by /root/b_message_review. Inspected current relevant guidance and retained failure evidence; independent analyst plus follow-up preserved continuation, integration, questions/timing and allocation distinctions. Substantial relevant source coverage is separate from dependable live behavior; no general internal cause, throughput advantage or behavioral repair established. Existing accepted message gate preserved; targeted live decision/action evaluation recommended before broad rewrite or new universal mechanism. No source/config activation, monitoring, thesis restart or substantial evaluation programme.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Jörn requested two new sessions on8October. Initial bounded investigation/problem development; no substantial execution, research restart or config authority inferred.\nnext_step: Initial assessment delivered for direct discussion. Broader behavioral reliability and measured review cost/benefit remain open; further evaluation is recommended, not launched or approved by this record.\nSources: docs/coordination/handoffs/20261008-ab-split/B-harness.md, docs/coordination/handoffs/20261008-ab-split/B-assessment.md, docs/coordination/message-reviews/2026-10-08/B-harness/final-v1.md, docs/coordination/message-reviews/2026-10-08/B-harness/final-v1-review.txt\n\n9 October agent-account session: Jörn FAIL verdict\nSession closed by Jörn as FAIL. Scientific account remains unfinished. Bounded failure/review/discovery archive retained on main and canonical incident intake saved; no follow-on execution or workflow acceptance.\nproject: msc-math\nauthorization: Jörn gave five minutes to wrap up and preserve anything worth merging to main.\nSources: docs/history/agent-account-session-failure-20261009/README.md"];
  "__parked" [label="UNSELECTED / PARKED · no execution\nCommunication diagnosis · BLOCKED\nSkill migration candidate · PARKED\nKnowledge cleanup / pilot · PARKED\nCloud automation · PARKED\nHistorical stop respected · DONE\nOptional result routes · PARKED\nOpen research packages · PARKED\nWriting method trial · PARKED\nDefine consequential friction and the stopping judgment · READY\nSpecify a comparison that can reject a candidate mechanism · READY\nCompare coordination at one integration boundary · READY\nSelect a version-aware per-thread prompt-composition view · READY\nLocal-maximality proofs and certificate navigation · DONE\nExact product-family proofs · DONE\nEmpirical interpretation and numerical example · DONE\nReproduction and evidence availability · DONE\nIndependent local-theorem review · DONE\nNumerical API-contract review · DONE", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#f1f0ed", color="#93918c", tooltip="Determine why agent communication tools failed\nBounded local diagnosis finished. Same daemon persisted through failures; multiple TUI MCP server processes turned over. Stale endpoint binding is plausible, but old-port ownership, shutdown/rebind evidence and original cause are unavailable. Current list verifies reads only.\nblocker: Historical endpoint ownership/binding evidence is unavailable; current successful reads do not establish original cause or legacy send recovery.\nplan_gap: Capture failing URL, socket owner/PID and endpoint-binding lifecycle events on the next natural failure. Do not launch repeated investigation or restart the shared daemon.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/current.json\n\nOptional local skill candidate, activation and fresh-client tests\nProposed nine-skill local package, Claude discovery adapters and focused acceptance route. Keep outside loaded paths until selected. This is a candidate route, not an assignment.\nplan_gap: Initial instruction was inspect/plan/discuss first; migration and activation selection absent.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/skill-migration-plan.md\n\nOptional knowledge cleanup and forward pilot\nChoose retain-and-observe, two-link cleanup only, or cleanup plus bounded A/E pilot. No model calls or cleanup are launched by this plan.\nplan_gap: Scope, owner and resources have not been selected; broader cases and post-compaction validation remain unperformed.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/knowledge-evaluation-plan.md\n\nPossible cloud communication, setup and accounting automation\nExternal surfaces remain outside workstation telemetry. Live cloud messaging, detailed returned event logs and enforcement are possible mechanisms; required support and value are undecided.\nplan_gap: No agreed need, design, acceptance contract or authorization for cloud automation.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/development-environments.md\n\nPrevious thesis stop superseded by 4 October authorization\nThe previous stop was respected until Jörn authorized this new bounded thesis/repository run. This historical task is closed; oct04-candidate owns current execution.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Historical stop respected until explicit restart; oct04-candidate owns current scope.\nSources: docs/coordination/handoff.md\n\nReview optional research/result selection\nHarmonic blind directions, ridge circulation, moment counterexample and joint-representation separations remain unselected. Symmetric-partner theorem moved to selected thesis scope on 3 October; presentation and proof acceptance remain open.\nplan_gap: Remaining optional results are unselected; the general zonotope bound remains conjectural/paused.\nproject: research\nauthorization: Unselected optional work; not a thesis-completion prerequisite or execution authorization.\nnext_step: Select a bounded statement/evidence/value comparison before any research execution or thesis addition.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md\n\nStructure a bounded future mathematical research packet\nThe dated scientific view records F=11/global HKO questions as outside the submission route; project facts distinguish non-generic arbitrary-polytope support from generic smooth-branch results. These are possible future questions, not current theorem obligations or assigned experiments.\nplan_gap: Exact question, owner evidence baseline, useful alternatives and resources have not been selected; recheck source owners before promoting historical open questions.\nproject: research\nauthorization: Unselected optional work; not a thesis-completion prerequisite or execution authorization.\nnext_step: Select a bounded problem-structuring packet; no large proof search, producer or Pro handoff follows automatically.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md, docs/dashboard/thesis.html\n\nConsider a discriminating authoring-workflow trial\nA current-source passage trial may inform authoring value, but local trials cannot certify whole-thesis readiness. Source repairs have independent value and do not depend on this optional mechanism.\nplan_gap: No trial candidate, success criterion, cost or human-review package selected; retrospective writing outcomes are not a general reliable method.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected optional work; not a thesis-completion prerequisite or execution authorization.\nnext_step: Select a concrete trial only if it could change the authoring route enough to justify its cost.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md\n\nDefine consequential friction and the stopping judgment\nOpen judgment about what costs matter for actual MSc project work, what constitutes repair success, and when further investment is worthwhile. No numeric target inferred from examples.\nplan_gap: No grounded baseline or agreed distinction between successful repair and justified stopping with unmet goals.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: 3 October authorized bounded brainstorming, source retrieval and information-producing probes. No substantial execution, host configuration change or thesis restart.\nnext_step: Discuss concrete project consequences and alternative stopping interpretations; this does not block unrelated bounded intake.\nSources: docs/coordination/goal-map.json, AGENTS.md.commentary.md\n\nSpecify a comparison that can reject a candidate mechanism\nCandidate bounded comparison on one source-grounded decision and later correction; fixture, receiving surface, observable outputs and integration owner not selected.\nplan_gap: Existing returns do not establish which discovery/application mechanism is worth deploying or whether an exact case is adequately reconstructable.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: 3 October authorized bounded brainstorming, source retrieval and information-producing probes. No substantial execution, host configuration change or thesis restart.\nnext_step: Choose a concrete case and a discriminating result before investing in implementation; include prior negative evidence and opportunity costs.\nSources: docs/coordination/problem-knowledge-interventions.md, docs/coordination/problem-knowledge-probe.md\n\nCompare coordination at one integration boundary\nCandidate interface rehearsal comparing central, peer and bounded-integrator arrangements. No clean retrospective topology comparison or superiority claim available.\nplan_gap: How coordination changes parent-context demands, unresolved obligations and human rescue is not measured.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: 3 October authorized bounded brainstorming, source retrieval and information-producing probes. No substantial execution, host configuration change or thesis restart.\nnext_step: If selected, compare handling of concurrent outputs, an unresolved integration obligation and a late correction; avoid three full project lifecycles.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md, docs/history/process-audit/REPORT.md, docs/coordination/goal-map.json\n\nSelect a version-aware per-thread prompt-composition view\nAccepted handoff from 01a102da-b805-7f72-ae02-ba9842fa80a8; receipt saved at /tmp/msc-math/prompt-view-handoff-receipt.txt; sender receipt is not established. Bounded inspection found native CODEX_ROLLOUT_TRACE_ROOT request bundles in pinned source. Installed activation, complete deferred inventory, provenance and partial/delta reconstruction remain unverified. Design at ~/.codex/artifacts/recurring-data-2026-10-03/prompt-view-design.txt.\nplan_gap: Full runtime capture and freshness/coverage contracts not yet exercised.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Receiving inspection/design only. Implementation, environment/config activation, paid capture, build and restart remain unselected; config implications stay with sender.\nnext_step: Locate one existing native bundle or propose a narrowly approved future capture; verify schema and gaps before choosing a renderer.\nSources: docs/codex.md\n\nLocal-maximality proofs and certificate navigation\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: thesis/chapters/07-hko.tex\n\nExact product-family proofs\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: thesis/chapters/09-rotated-regular-polygons.tex, thesis/chapters/10-affine-pentagons.tex, thesis/chapters/11-product-position.tex\n\nEmpirical interpretation and numerical example\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: thesis/chapters/08-data-science.tex, thesis/chapters/13-numerics.tex\n\nReproduction and evidence availability\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: thesis/chapters/14-code-data.tex, INSTALL.md\n\nIndependent local-theorem review\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Original task stopped; no running assignment.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: docs/coordination/restart-2026-10-04.md\n\nNumerical API-contract review\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Original task stopped; no running assignment.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: docs/coordination/restart-2026-10-04.md"];
  "__candidates_thesis" [label="THESIS · READY IF SELECTED\nFoundations / QP\nVariation / certificate\nProduct proof bridges\nDS reader disposition\nFigures / numerical example\nAI reflection map", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#fff7dc", color="#93918c", tooltip="Check current foundations and QP exposition\nRead Chapters 2 and 4 against backlog items 1: terminology, Rudolf input/output, cyclic-word operation and dependence/vertex-replacement bridges. Return surviving/solved/withdrawn findings with exact source locations; no edits or theorem strengthening.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded read-only Chapter 2/4 packet in its own worktree.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md\n\nCheck variation and HKO certificate navigation\nRead Chapters 6/7 and HKO appendix against backlog item 2; separate finite predicates and geometric implication. The certificate and slope-to-neighborhood proof are reported present. No certificate recomputation.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded source-navigation review; coordinate Chapter 7 edits with the claim packet.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md\n\nCheck product-family finite and limiting proof bridges\nRead Chapters 9–11 against backlog item 3: ordered pairings, finite vertex/alternation calculations, equality classification, product-position squeeze and Hausdorff/capacity-continuity bridge. Preserve exact/numerical distinctions.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select an independent product-proof source packet; report exact surviving bridges before edits.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md\n\nDispose of reader concerns against the selected DS chapter\nMap retained human comments to current Chapter 8/appendix: applied, absent, context-accepted or older-draft-only. Preserve accepted correlation/area text, retrospective bounds and explicitly unresolved random_F8_s3_45. Human acceptance and overall DS scope remain separate.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a source-aware DS disposition packet; do not import old rejection as a current verdict.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md\n\nCheck visualization purposes and certified numerical example\nInspect Chapters 12–14 for panel purpose/inference limits and the requested concrete certified numerical example; return a scoped proposal using existing code/evidence without launching producers.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a read-only example/provenance design packet before implementing or running it.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md\n\nVerify AI annotation repairs against the selected source\nCheck selected Chapter 15 against the mapped v3 repairs; no confirmed annotation defect remains. Preserve factual disclosure separately from reflection and record source drift or unknown whole-chapter acceptance.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded source-map check; do not rewrite unflagged AI prose.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md"];
  "__candidates_evidence" [label="EVIDENCE · READY IF SELECTED\nChapter 7 claim check\nCode correspondence\nArtifact traceability", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#fff7dc", color="#93918c", tooltip="Check rendered Chapter 7 claims and PDF/source identity\nIdentify source revision/PDF identity, then compare L10-N/L10-N+ rendered statement, equality family and upper-section-curvature caveat against 24 September disposition and non-HKO rational/analytic packet. If no matching PDF is available, report that prerequisite; do not treat the older frozen PDF as current.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: evidence\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select the bounded rendered-PDF claim audit; no expensive verifier rerun.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/consolidation/2026-09-24/claim-disposition.md, experiments/hko-local-maximum/non-hko/README.md, experiments/hko-local-maximum/non-hko/PROOF.md\n\nCheck retained algorithm and numerical contract boundaries\nTrace retained capacity/numerics/flow promises to crate APIs and focused evidence owners; distinguish theorem assumptions, bounded tests and optimized production correspondence. Return exact claim/contract gaps and recommended focused checks; no blanket implementation rewrite.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: evidence\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select read-only claim/API/evidence mapping in a separate worktree; test execution requires its chosen packet.\nSources: crates/README.md, docs/project-facts.md, ARCHITECTURE.md\n\nResolve displayed examples, counts and public artifact references\nMap named KKT/comparison/product counts, figures and annotated HKO listing to canonical packets and actual tracked/registered/public availability. Existing local files do not establish a public commit or remote download promise.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: evidence\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded current-claim-to-artifact inventory; preserve producer-owned outputs.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md"];
  "__candidates_reproduction" [label="REPRODUCTION · READY IF SELECTED\nReproduction inventory", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#fff7dc", color="#93918c", tooltip="Compare the reproduction playbook with retained thesis promises\nSelected13figure producer/input/publication-copy/PDF routes now mapped and executed, with versions, comparisons and explicit limits. Remaining opportunity concerns full historical producer, LICCA hardware/timing and long-horizon reproduction coverage.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: reproduction\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Keep remaining full-producer/long-horizon scope separate from completed selected-figure route.\nSources: docs/figure-reproduction.md, docs/reproducibility.md"];
  "__candidates_release" [label="RELEASE · READY IF SELECTED\nOfficial status check\nArchive preparation", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#fff7dc", color="#93918c", tooltip="Establish current submission status and official requirements\nPrepare a bounded check of current submission status, official rules and AI-disclosure requirements. Ask Jörn/current official sources when selected; never infer remaining hand-in or missed deadlines from historical notes.\nplan_gap: Unassigned and unselected; current administration/closure facts need inspection.\nproject: release\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select current status/rules inquiry; no external submission or message is authorized.\nSources: docs/project-facts.md, docs/coordination/handoff.md\n\nInventory closure-time rights, data and archive gaps\nCompare current payload/registry to accepted continuation/Zenodo checklist: rights notices, private/disposable material, useful artifacts, clean-cache materialization, exact reviewed commit/PDF, metadata and exterior publication. Return dispositions/questions without deleting, packing or publishing.\nplan_gap: Unassigned and unselected; current administration/closure facts need inspection.\nproject: release\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded read-only closure inventory in its own worktree.\nSources: submit/archive-closure-checklist.md, docs/project-facts.md"];
